# Realtime Patterns (ws-nitro transport)

This project's chat transport is **`ws-nitro`**: Nitro's `defineWebSocketHandler` at `/_ws`, gated by `nitro.experimental.websocket = true` (set automatically by the chat feature). Other realtime needs should use the same pattern.

**SSE / server-pushed events**: documented below as a reference pattern but ⚠️ **currently broken under Cloudflare** (edge proxy buffers `text/event-stream` and chunked-transfer responses, defeating incremental streaming). Safe to use only when the deployment target is *not* Cloudflare-fronted, or when the SSE-buffering behaviour gets resolved upstream. For LLM streaming + chat → use the WebSocket transport.

## Adding a WebSocket route

```ts
// server/routes/_ws-<name>.ts
export default defineWebSocketHandler({
    async open(peer) {
        // peer.send(...) any time
    },
    async message(peer, message) {
        const payload = JSON.parse(typeof message === 'string' ? message : message.text())
        // process and respond
        peer.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'ack' }))
    },
    async close(peer) {
        // cleanup
    },
})
```

Auth: Nitro middleware runs before the upgrade; `requireUserSession(peer.context.event)` works the same as in HTTP routes (Nitro 2 + Nuxt 4 experimental).

## PG LISTEN/NOTIFY (server-pushed updates)

For data-change push, pair the WS route with PostgreSQL LISTEN/NOTIFY:

```ts
// server/plugins/realtime.ts — set up LISTEN once at server start
import postgres from 'postgres'

const peers = new Set<any>()

export default defineNitroPlugin(() => {
    const sql = postgres(String(useRuntimeConfig().databaseUrl))
    sql.listen('data_changed', (payload) => {
        for (const peer of peers) peer.send(payload)
    })
})
```

```ts
// server/routes/_ws-events.ts
export default defineWebSocketHandler({
    open(peer) { peers.add(peer) },
    close(peer) { peers.delete(peer) },
})
```

```ts
// notify after a mutation
import postgres from 'postgres'
const sql = postgres(String(useRuntimeConfig().databaseUrl))
await sql.notify('data_changed', JSON.stringify({ table: 'todos', id }))
```

LISTEN requires a **dedicated connection**; don't reuse the Drizzle query pool.

## Client side

```ts
const url = new URL('/_ws', window.location.href)
url.protocol = url.protocol === 'https:' ? 'wss:' : 'ws:'
const ws = new WebSocket(url.toString())
```

Reconnect on close (exponential backoff capped at ~30s). Don't reconnect after intentional `close()`; set `ws.onclose = null` first.

## SSE pattern (reference only, ⚠️ broken under Cloudflare)

> ⚠️ **Status: not supported in production today.** Cloudflare's edge proxy buffers `text/event-stream` and chunked-transfer responses below ~100 KB, so incremental events arrive in batches several seconds late. We don't ship an SSE-based chat transport for that reason. Keep this section as a reference pattern only: if your project is *not* Cloudflare-fronted (direct nginx, Vercel, Fly.io) and you genuinely want one-way push, the code below is the shape it would take. If/when Cloudflare buffering gets fixed (or you set `Cache-Control: no-transform` on a non-buffered route), re-evaluate.

### Server: streaming API route

```ts
// server/api/events.get.ts
import postgres from 'postgres'

export default defineEventHandler(async (event) => {
    setResponseHeader(event, 'content-type', 'text/event-stream')
    setResponseHeader(event, 'cache-control', 'no-cache, no-transform')
    setResponseHeader(event, 'connection', 'keep-alive')

    const sql = postgres(String(useRuntimeConfig().databaseUrl))

    await sql.listen('data_changed', (payload) => {
        event.node.res.write(`data: ${payload}\n\n`)
    })

    event._handled = true

    event.node.req.on('close', () => sql.end())
})
```

### Client: composable

```ts
// app/composables/useSSE.ts
export function useSSE<T>(url: string, channel?: string) {
    const data = ref<T | null>(null)
    let eventSource: EventSource | null = null

    onMounted(() => {
        eventSource = new EventSource(url)
        eventSource.onmessage = (event) => {
            const parsed = JSON.parse(event.data)
            if (!channel || parsed.table === channel) data.value = parsed
        }
    })

    onUnmounted(() => eventSource?.close())

    return { data }
}
```

For LLM streaming + chat: use the WebSocket transport. SSE is reserved for future / non-Cloudflare deploys only.
